# The eye test that cannot lie about WHO drew it.
#
# Summoned by a LONE decorator line, no data to improvise:
#
#   @{view:eyetest, tone:gold}
#
# Only this folder carries this view, and the box names itself, so the screen tells
# you which engine answered:
#
#   a coloured box saying sandbox/node_modules  -> the TARBALL drew it, verdict valid
#   a raw decorator line                        -> no hook ran, or an engine without
#                                                  this view won the message
#   a literal "@tone" line, or a visible tag    -> an engine too old for the tone
#                                                  slot drew it
#
# The last case is the one that used to fool a reader: a user-scoped plugin's hook
# fires here too, and it draws with ITS OWN engine and views.
@tone key
@box
@head {{tone}}EYE TEST{{/}}
@right sandbox/views/eyetest.view
Drawn by the tarball installed in `sandbox/node_modules`, from this folder's
own view. No plugin ships this file, so nothing else can have rendered it.
@rule
 {{tone}}TONE{{/}}  {{tone}}▎{{/}} this line spends the tone slot, so the colour
 {{tone}}    {{/}}  {{tone}}▎{{/}} you see is the class the decorator named
 {{tone}}    {{/}}  {{tone}}▎{{/}} (`tone:gold` renders gold, no attribute renders key)
@endbox
